      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Today, @USCG announced homeporting locations for three Arctic Security Cutters (ASC) in the State of Alaska. The first two ASCs will be homeported in Kodiak, with a third ASC to be homeported in Seward when the infrastructure is ready. Strategically positioning these state-of-the-art icebreakers in Alaska will maximize our ability to defend our northern border and approaches, while reinforcing America’s maritime dominance in a crucial region of strategic importance. Fueled by $3.5B in FY25 reconciliation funding, the Coast Guard’s acquisition of ASCs continues an historic expansion of our nation’s icebreaker fleet, and underscores the United States’ leadership as a maritime power in the Arctic.\n\nRead more here: https://t.co/sz3FHT1l8K",
      "text_resolved": "Today, @USCG announced homeporting locations for three Arctic Security Cutters (ASC) in the State of Alaska. The first two ASCs will be homeported in Kodiak, with a third ASC to be homeported in Seward when the infrastructure is ready. Strategically positioning these state-of-the-art icebreakers in Alaska will maximize our ability to defend our northern border and approaches, while reinforcing America’s maritime dominance in a crucial region of strategic importance. Fueled by $3.5B in FY25 reconciliation funding, the Coast Guard’s acquisition of ASCs continues an historic expansion of our nation’s icebreaker fleet, and underscores the United States’ leadership as a maritime power in the Arctic.\n\nRead more here: https://tinyurl.com/y4w58kx6",
