      "text": "Fleet recapitalization continues as @USCG accepted delivery of the 63rd FRC, CGC Jeffrey Palazzo, in Key West, FL. Following a commissioning in September 2026, the cutter will homeport in Guam for western Pacific operations, maintaining steady patrol boat capabilities.\n\nThe vessel honors Coast Guard Reserve Petty Officer 1st Class Jeffrey Palazzo, an 8-year veteran of CGC Cape Horn and Station Chatham who later joined FDNY Rescue Squad 5 and lost his life responding on 9/11.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/miFCDjbE4A",
