      "text": "@USCG has awarded two task orders totaling over $143M to deliver 30 housing units, a child development center, and a recapitalized water storage tank at Base Kodiak. Leveraging historic investment in the FY25 reconciliation funding, these projects will expand access to quality housing, modern facilities, and essential services for Coast Guard personnel and families.\n\nBase Kodiak is the Coast Guard’s largest operational facility and a critical provider of U.S. presence and capability in the Arctic region, supporting both surface and aviation operations.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/V7uUyNhd27",
      "text_resolved": "@USCG has awarded two task orders totaling over $143M to deliver 30 housing units, a child development center, and a recapitalized water storage tank at Base Kodiak. Leveraging historic investment in the FY25 reconciliation funding, these projects will expand access to quality housing, modern facilities, and essential services for Coast Guard personnel and families.\n\nBase Kodiak is the Coast Guard’s largest operational facility and a critical provider of U.S. presence and capability in the Arctic region, supporting both surface and aviation operations.\n\nRead more: https://tinyurl.com/4ra4dmtf",
